**SQL injection.** `req.params.id` goes raw into query string. Attacker sends `1 OR 1=1` → dumps all users. `1; DROP TABLE users` → gone.

**Fix — parameterized query:**

```js
app.get('/api/users/:id', async (req, res) => {
  const { id } = req.params;
  if (!/^\d+$/.test(id)) return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid id' });

  try {
    const user = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1', [id]);
    if (!user.rows.length) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' });
    res.json(user.rows[0]);
  } catch {
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Server error' });
  }
});
```

**Other issues:**

| Issue | Risk | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| No auth check | Any user fetch any user | Add session/JWT middleware |
| `SELECT *` | Leaks password hash, internal fields | Explicit column list |
| No 404 handling | Reveals DB absence vs error | Check `rows.length` |
| No error handling | Stack trace leaks on crash | `try/catch` |

Param binding (`$1`) is non-negotiable — DB driver escapes it, injection impossible.
